# Security headers for intersecting-parallels.pages.dev — Doctrine §16.6
#
# The four the whole family ships, plus a Content-Security-Policy the hub
# cannot have: this placeholder carries ZERO script, so default-src 'none' is
# free today. style-src 'unsafe-inline' covers the page's inline <style>; with
# no script allowed at all, that is a small concession.
#
# HONESTY NOTE for the session that ships the real app: the app will almost
# certainly carry inline script and a service worker, and this CSP will block
# both. REVISIT IT DELIBERATELY in that commit — loosen it and say so, or
# extract scripts and keep it. Do not let the first broken deploy be the way
# anyone finds out it was here.
#
# No Strict-Transport-Security: pages.dev is HTTPS-only and Cloudflare handles
# TLS; a lock-in header that cannot be tested from here would be worse than
# leaving it to the platform.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
